WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.053
Copyright and licensing affect how material may be copied, adapted and shared.

00:00:05.053 --> 00:00:09.685
Attribution identifies a source but does not by itself grant permission.

00:00:09.685 --> 00:00:17.685
A licence states conditions under which use is allowed; different licences can impose different requirements on redistribution and modification.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.043
No.

00:00:19.043 --> 00:00:21.547
Credit is not the same as permission.

00:00:21.547 --> 00:00:27.628
The teacher must check the applicable licence, permission or legal exception and use an allowed sharing method.

00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:31.920
Linking to an authorised public video can differ from redistributing a copy.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.754
Does attribution alone always permit redistribution?

00:00:35.754 --> 00:00:41.895
Permission depends on the licence or another applicable legal basis, not attribution alone.
